, I so pose, for normal procedure. She was just <b>given</b> True Fae rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T00:16:21-08:00","id":348871,"title":"","content":"Equinox road suggests that every changeling in Arcadia becomes fully fae at a moment. However to keep with your example, no the only system given is the conversion Changeling/True Fae with an escaped Changeling.<br /> <br /> Still always possibilities<br /> <br /> A changeling can be hollowed by her master and made the recipient of a Title, she becomes a part of her master.<br /> <br /> or Many mortals are kidnapped and reshaped in Whisps the retinue of a Fae Lord","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T00:42:11-08:00","id":348876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/348832-from-changeling-to-true-fae?p=348868#post348868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But can character be <b>granted</b> a True Fae status? ( The Title thing, probably? )</div> </div> </div> </div>Titles are massive Contracts with the Wyrd that the Fae express their identities through and functionally amount to a portfolio of symbolism they can leverage, in contrast to their Names, which define their ultimate identity and pick up bits of every Title they've ever held in the event that they wind up with no Titles and have to play their games in the comparative poverty of a single individual manifestation. Being &quot;granted&quot; a Title would amount to being incorporated into an existing Fae (sometimes abandoned Titles simply <i>sprout a new Fae on their own</i>). The nearest the Lost get to the concept is the higher accorded respect the Others give to changelings who are part of Entitlements and the rumor that the founders of the Seasonal Courts managed to claim Titles without becoming Fae first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T01:20:46-08:00","id":348886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/348832-from-changeling-to-true-fae?p=348876#post348876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being &quot;granted&quot; a Title would amount to being incorporated into an existing Fae (sometimes abandoned Titles simply <i>sprout a new Fae on their own</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>It does sound like in the <i>Books of Faerie</i> - <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Rosebed become Titania, Queen of Fearie, when she marries King-Regent Obrey.</div></div> </div> </div> She helt her position as Queen of Faerie when she marries the Auberon, correct King of Faerie - that himself took mark of King of Faerie by killing in honroble battle the Obrey, King Regent.<br /> <br /> Is King and Queen of Faerie good examples of Title in working? If yes, now I does understand how <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/314862-krampus-in-ctl?p=315272#post315272\">Santa Claus and Krampus could be two True Fae sharing on Title</a>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T03:47:34-08:00","id":348936,"title":"","content":"Seriously, read the books first because they have rules already. Once that's finished you can start playing around with rules that the authors provided because that's easier than devising from scratch. Otherwise it feels like putting the cart before the horse to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}